{"name":"Plantation Shutters","hex":"#6a5143","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plantation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large farm; estate or area of land designated for agricultural growth. Often includes housing for the owner and workers.","An area where trees are planted, either for commercial purposes, or to adorn an estate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plantation"},{"term":"shutters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shutter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shutters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window shutter","blocks":[{"text":"A window shutter is a solid and stable window covering, usually consisting of a frame of vertical stiles and horizontal rails. Set within this frame can be louvers, solid panels, fabric, glass and almost any other item that can be mounted within a frame.\nShutters may be employed for a variety of reasons, including controlling the amount of sunlight that enters a room, to provide privacy, security, to protect against weather or unwanted intrusion or damage and to enhance the aesthetics of a building."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Interior-Shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_shutter","wikidata":"Q1096423"},{"title":"Plantation","blocks":[{"text":"Plantations are farms specializing in cash crops, usually mainly planting a single crop, with perhaps ancillary areas for vegetables for eating and so on. Plantations, centered on a plantation house, grow crops including cotton, cannabis, tobacco, coffee, tea, cocoa, sugar cane, opium, coca, sisal, oil seeds, oil palms, fruits, rubber trees and forest trees. Plantation crops are grown on large lands called estates. These crops are grown with scientific methods and a large, highly skilled labor force. Crops such as tea and coffee are grown on hillslopes as they cannot withstand stagnant water. Protectionist policies and natural comparative advantage have sometimes contributed to determining where plantations are located."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Los-esclavos-en-cuba-1.jpg/330px-Los-esclavos-en-cuba-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plantation","wikidata":"Q188913"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern interior wooden window shutters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindow_shutters.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/500px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/1280px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/500px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Workers installing plantation-style shutters in a home.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorkers_installing_shutters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg/500px-Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg/1280px-Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg/500px-Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shutters in Aix-en-Provence, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg/500px-Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg/1280px-Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg/500px-Fenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brightly colored shutters in Romania","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFenetre_bleue_Jurilovca_Musee_Village_Bucarest.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg/500px-Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg/1280px-Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg/500px-Okiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One side shutters in Poland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOkiennica_-_window_shutter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG/500px-French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG/1280px-French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG/500px-French_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shutters are frequently seen in French-influenced architecture.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrench_Concession_building_-_Shanghai.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG/500px-Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG/1280px-Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG/500px-Dinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The old town of Dinkelsbühl, Germany, completely consists of houses with colored exterior shutters.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADinkelsbuehl_BW_8.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sugar_cane_workers_resting_1a34016v.jpg/500px-Sugar_cane_workers_resting_1a34016v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sugar_cane_workers_resting_1a34016v.jpg/50